        ":question/id": "7de40719-e1b7-5230-a137-1dc3c55de0ef",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-72763",
        ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M,$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ on $M?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the first row to the third row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1+(-1)(1) & -1+(-1)(0) & 1+(-1)(2) & 2+(-1)(3)\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
