        ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ on $X?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the first row to the second row. \n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1+(-1)(1) & 5+(-1)(3) & -1+(-1)(2) & 2+(-1)(1) \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"
