        ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $N,$ given by\n\n$$\nN=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ on $N?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $-2$ times the first row to the second row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2+(-2)(1) & 1+(-2)(-2) & 2+(-2)(1) & 3+(-2)(-1) \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"
